(12567,'Drupal API Usage','','11.4.11'),
(12568,'Analysis of Drupal Core APIs used in custom code: hooks, preprocess functions, event subscribers, and global functions.','','11.4.11'),
(12569,'These expectations describe what a correct configuration looks like on this environment. They are the single source for two things: the score of this audit, and the \"Audit: configuration checks\" summary block. Both read the same list, so the report and the block can never disagree.','','11.4.11'),
(12570,'Because the list is configuration, every project and every environment declares its own rules, for core, contrib or custom modules alike. For example: CSS and JS aggregation must be enabled in production; the Devel module must not be installed in production but must be installed on a development environment; a project specific custom module must stay enabled here.','','11.4.11'),
(12571,'And because it is a plain configuration object, it can be overridden per environment like any other: assign <code>@override</code> in <code>settings.php</code>, or ship a different version of that configuration from a Config Split. The checks then run against the overridden values.','','11.4.11'),
(12572,'Module recommendations for <strong>@categories</strong> are active because their audit submodules are enabled.','','11.4.11'),
