(12589,'Directories to scan','','11.4.11'),
(12590,'Enter one directory path per line, relative to the project root (e.g., web/modules/custom). These directories will be scanned by analyzers that perform code analysis (Performance, Twig, PHPStan, PHPCS, Rector, etc.). They must stay inside the project: paths with \"..\" and absolute paths outside it are not allowed.','','11.4.11'),
(12591,'Exclude patterns','','11.4.11'),
(12592,'Enter one pattern per line. Files or directories matching these patterns will be excluded from scanning (e.g., *Test.php, tests/, node_modules/).','','11.4.11'),
(12593,'Static rule overrides','','11.4.11'),
(12594,'Disable a code rule of the Security, Performance, Cache or Twig audit, or change its severity, for the whole site or for some paths. One override per line: <code>RULE_ID [PATH_PATTERN] SEVERITY</code>, where SEVERITY is error, warning, notice or disabled and PATH_PATTERN is matched against the file path relative to the project root (<code>*</code> also matches <code>/</code>). Rule IDs are the finding codes shown in the reports. When several lines match, the last one wins. Example: <code>CACHE_MAX_AGE_ZERO */src/Controller/Admin* notice</code>','','11.4.11'),
(12595,'Modules allowed to be enabled','','11.4.11'),
(12596,'Development or risky modules that this site keeps enabled on purpose, one machine name per line (e.g. devel). They are still listed in the Modules and Performance audits, as acknowledged information, but no longer count as problems. To allow a module on development environments only, set this value in settings.php: <code>$config[\'audit.settings\'][\'allowed_modules\'] = \"devel\";</code>','','11.4.11'),
(12597,'Accept configuration overridden only in this environment','','11.4.11'),
(12598,'For development environments that override configuration on purpose (for example DDEV sets the error level to verbose). Findings caused by such an override, such as visible error messages or disabled CSS/JS aggregation, are listed as acknowledged information when the stored configuration is production-safe; when the stored value fails too, they keep their severity. Enable it in the settings.php of that environment, never in exported configuration: <code>@code</code>','','11.4.11'),
(12599,'Execution timeout (seconds)','','11.4.11'),
(12600,'Maximum time for external tools (PHPCS, PHPStan, phploc) to complete analysis. <strong>Recommended: 60 seconds.</strong> Increase for very large codebases. Also limited by PHP max_execution_time.','','11.4.11'),
(12601,'0 - Excluded','','11.4.11'),
(12602,'1 - Low','','11.4.11'),
(12603,'2 - Below Average','','11.4.11'),
(12604,'3 - Average','','11.4.11'),
(12605,'4 - Above Average','','11.4.11'),
(12606,'5 - Critical','','11.4.11'),
(12607,'Project Score Multipliers','','11.4.11'),
(12608,'These multipliers determine how each audit contributes to the <strong>overall Project Score</strong> displayed on the audit overview page. The Project Score is calculated as a weighted average: audits with higher multipliers have more influence on the final score. For example, if \"Updates\" has a multiplier of 5 (Critical) and \"Twig\" has a multiplier of 2 (Low), security updates will affect the Project Score 2.5 times more than Twig issues. Set a multiplier to 0 to completely exclude that audit from the Project Score calculation.','','11.4.11'),
(12609,'General Settings','','11.4.11'),
(12610,'Ignore cache bin analysis','','11.4.11'),
(12611,'Skip analysis of cache bin inventory and backend assignments.','','11.4.11'),
(12612,'Ignore cache backend analysis','','11.4.11'),
(12613,'Skip the whole cache backend section: default backend, Redis/Memcache and page cache checks.','','11.4.11'),
(12614,'Accept the database cache backend (no Redis/Memcache)','','11.4.11'),
(12615,'For sites where database-only caching is intentional: the database backend and missing Redis/Memcache findings are listed as acknowledged information and do not affect the score. The page cache checks still run.','','11.4.11'),
(12616,'Ignore cache tag usage analysis','','11.4.11'),
(12617,'Skip analysis of cache tag usage patterns in custom code.','','11.4.11'),
(12618,'Ignore cache tag invalidation analysis','','11.4.11'),
(12619,'Skip snapshot-based analysis of cache tag invalidation frequency from the cachetags table. When enabled, a snapshot is saved every 12 hours to calculate deltas.','','11.4.11'),
(12620,'Paths to analyze and exclude patterns are configured in the <a href=\":url\">main audit settings</a> (scan_directories and exclude_patterns).','','11.4.11'),
(12621,'Include test files','','11.4.11'),
(12622,'Include test files in analysis. Not recommended - tests have different complexity patterns.','','11.4.11'),
(12623,'Analysis Scope','','11.4.11'),
(12624,'CCN warning threshold','','11.4.11'),
(12625,'Functions with cyclomatic complexity above this value will generate warnings. <strong>Recommended: 10</strong>','','11.4.11'),
(12626,'CCN error threshold','','11.4.11'),
(12627,'Functions with cyclomatic complexity above this value will generate errors. <strong>Recommended: 20</strong>','','11.4.11'),
(12628,'Maintainability index warning threshold','','11.4.11'),
(12629,'Functions with a maintainability index below this value will generate warnings. The index is on a 0-100 scale (higher is better) and combines the Halstead volume, lines of code and cyclomatic complexity of each function. <strong>Recommended: 40</strong>','','11.4.11'),
(12630,'Maintainability index error threshold','','11.4.11'),
(12631,'Functions with a maintainability index below this value will generate errors. Same 0-100 scale as the warning threshold (Halstead volume, lines of code and cyclomatic complexity). <strong>Recommended: 20</strong>','','11.4.11'),
(12632,'Deep array threshold','','11.4.11'),
(12633,'Arrays nested deeper than this level will be flagged. Recommended: 5 (Drupal render arrays commonly use 3-4 levels, so 5 avoids false positives).','','11.4.11'),
(12634,'Complexity Thresholds','','11.4.11'),
(12635,'Detect service locators','','11.4.11'),
(12636,'Flag usage of \\Drupal::service() and similar static calls. Use dependency injection instead.','','11.4.11'),
(12637,'Allow service locators in procedural files','','11.4.11'),
(12638,'When enabled, \\Drupal:: calls in .module, .install, .theme, .inc, .profile, .deploy.php, and .post_update.php files will not be flagged. These files often cannot use dependency injection.','','11.4.11'),
(12639,'Detect deep array nesting','','11.4.11'),
(12640,'Flag arrays with excessive nesting levels.','','11.4.11'),
(12641,'Detect hardcoded entity IDs','','11.4.11'),
(12642,'Flag hardcoded numeric IDs in entity load calls.','','11.4.11'),
(12643,'Detect direct database queries','','11.4.11'),
(12644,'Flag usage of deprecated db_query() and similar functions.','','11.4.11'),
(12645,'Detect dynamic low-level render keys','','11.4.11'),
(12646,'Flag dynamic values assigned to #markup or #children. Use #theme or #type with a template instead.','','11.4.11'),
(12647,'Detect global variables','','11.4.11'),
(12648,'Flag usage of the global keyword. Inject the needed service or value instead.','','11.4.11'),
(12649,'Detect error suppression','','11.4.11'),
(12650,'Flag function calls silenced with the @ operator (trigger_error() is allowed).','','11.4.11'),
(12651,'Anti-Pattern Detection','','11.4.11'),
(12652,'Maximum hotspots to display','','11.4.11'),
(12653,'Limit the number of complexity hotspots shown. <strong>Recommended: 20</strong>','','11.4.11'),
(12654,'Execution timeout is configured globally in the <a href=\":url\">main audit settings</a>.','','11.4.11'),
(12655,'One expectation per line, in the format <code>config.object:key = expected value</code>. Use <code>!=</code> instead of <code>=</code> when any other value is acceptable, for instance <code>system.performance:cache.page.max_age != 0</code> to require that page caching is on whatever its lifetime. Values are compared as text: use <code>true</code> / <code>false</code> for booleans. Values of keys that look like secrets (passwords, tokens, API keys, salts), or of mappings that contain one, are compared but shown as (hidden) in the report. Lines starting with # are comments.','','11.4.11'),
(12656,'Modules that must be installed','','11.4.11'),
(12657,'One module machine name per line.','','11.4.11'),
(12658,'Modules that must not be installed','','11.4.11'),
(12659,'One module machine name per line. Development modules belong here.','','11.4.11'),
(12660,'Maximum hours without cron execution','','11.4.11'),
(12661,'If cron has not run in this many hours, an error will be shown. Set to 0 to disable this check.','','11.4.11'),
(12662,'Queue items warning threshold','','11.4.11'),
(12663,'If a queue has more than this many pending items, a warning will be shown. Set to 0 to disable this check.','','11.4.11'),
(12664,'Table size threshold (MB)','','11.4.11'),
(12665,'Tables exceeding this size will be flagged as warnings. Recommended: 50-100 MB (small sites), 100-500 MB (medium), 500-2000 MB (large).','','11.4.11'),
(12666,'Total database size threshold (MB)','','11.4.11'),
(12667,'Total database size exceeding this value will be flagged. Recommended: 500-1000 MB (small), 1000-5000 MB (medium), 5000-50000 MB (large).','','11.4.11'),
(12668,'Ignore cache backend warnings (no Redis/Memcache)','','11.4.11'),
(12669,'When enabled, the audit will not penalize the score for missing external cache backends (Redis or Memcache). Use this for sites where database-only caching is intentional and acceptable. The Cache Audit has its own setting for its Redis/Memcache warnings.','','11.4.11'),
(12670,'Ignore database logging (dblog) warnings','','11.4.11'),
(12671,'When enabled, the audit will not penalize the score for using database logging without syslog. Use this for sites where database logging is intentionally kept active.','','11.4.11'),
(12672,'Minimum duplicated lines','','11.4.11'),
(12673,'Minimum number of consecutive lines to consider as a clone. Lower values find more clones but increase false positives.','','11.4.11'),
(12674,'Minimum duplicated tokens','','11.4.11'),
(12675,'Minimum number of tokens (code units) in a clone block. Token-based matching is more accurate than line-based.','','11.4.11'),
(12676,'PHP (.php, .module, .install, .theme, .inc, .profile)','','11.4.11'),
(12677,'Twig templates (.twig)','','11.4.11'),
(12678,'JavaScript (.js)','','11.4.11'),
(12679,'CSS (.css)','','11.4.11'),
(12680,'File Formats','','11.4.11'),
(12681,'Maximum clones to display','','11.4.11'),
(12682,'Limits the number of clone pairs shown in the report. Does not affect score calculation.','','11.4.11'),
(12683,'Execution timeout is configured in the <a href=\":url\">main audit settings</a> (execution_timeout). Default is @default seconds — increase for large codebases.','','11.4.11'),
(12684,'Empty bundle threshold','','11.4.11'),
(12685,'Minimum entities required for a bundle to not be considered empty.','','11.4.11'),
(12686,'Bundles allowed to be empty','','11.4.11'),
(12687,'Bundles that are legitimately empty on this site, such as transactional or user-generated content (orders, profiles, comments), one per line as entity_type:bundle, or entity_type:* for all bundles of an entity type. They are listed as acknowledged information and do not affect the score.','','11.4.11'),
(12688,'Node revision threshold','','11.4.11'),
(12689,'Flag nodes with more revisions than this.','','11.4.11'),
(12690,'Paragraph revision threshold','','11.4.11'),
(12691,'Revision tables size threshold (MB)','','11.4.11'),
(12692,'Flag if revision tables exceed this size.','','11.4.11'),
(12693,'Maximum fields per bundle','','11.4.11'),
(12694,'Maximum recommended fields per bundle. Guidelines: Simple sites: 15-20 | Medium sites: 25-35 | Complex sites: 40-50','','11.4.11'),
(12695,'Maximum view modes per bundle','','11.4.11'),
(12696,'Maximum active view modes per bundle. Guidelines: Simple sites: 2-3 | Medium sites: 4-6 | Component-based: 8-12','','11.4.11'),
(12697,'Maximum form modes per bundle','','11.4.11'),
(12698,'Maximum active form modes per bundle. Most sites only need 1-2.','','11.4.11'),
(12699,'Fields allowed to be hidden','','11.4.11'),
(12700,'Fields that are hidden in every view mode or form mode on purpose, because their values are read in preprocess functions or templates, rendered through Views, or kept as data, one per line as entity_type:bundle:field_name. Use * as the bundle for all bundles of an entity type (for example paragraph:*:field_anchor). They are listed as acknowledged information and do not affect the score.','','11.4.11'),
(12701,'Minimum translation percentage','','11.4.11'),
(12702,'Minimum required interface translation coverage for each language whose interface is translated (every non-English language, and English only when English translation is enabled). Recommended: 80% minimum for production, 100% ideal. Languages below this threshold will be flagged. Full translation coverage is easily achievable today using AI-powered automated translation tools.','','11.4.11'),
(12703,'Analyze multilingual SEO configuration','','11.4.11'),
(12704,'When enabled, analyzes SEO-related configurations for multilingual sites. Disable this if SEO is not a priority for your site.','','11.4.11'),
(12705,'Require responsive images','','11.4.11'),
(12706,'Uncheck for projects that deliberately use plain image styles: the missing Responsive Image module and image fields without responsive images are then not reported. Image fields without any style are still reported.','','11.4.11'),
(12707,'Maximum recommended menu depth','','11.4.11'),
(12708,'Menus with items deeper than this will be flagged. Top-level links are at depth 1, as in the Drupal menu settings.','','11.4.11'),
(12709,'Excluded menus','','11.4.11'),
(12710,'Menu machine names left out of the audit, one per line. The Administration menu (admin) is generated by modules such as Admin Toolbar and Commerce; its depth is not an information architecture decision of the site.','','11.4.11'),
(12711,'No server-level cache services available (shared hosting, local or test environment)','','11.4.11'),
(12712,'Check this when the environment cannot run server-level cache services, such as shared hosting or a local or test environment. This will skip recommendations for advanced caching services (Memcache, Redis, Varnish) that require server-level installation.','','11.4.11'),
(12713,'Ignored module recommendations','','11.4.11'),
(12714,'Machine names of recommended modules this site does not need, one per line (for example responsive_image). They are listed as acknowledged information and do not affect the score. Metatag, Schema.org Metatag, Pathauto, Redirect and Simple XML Sitemap also follow the matching \"ignore\" settings of the SEO audit, and Responsive Image the \"Require responsive images\" setting of the Images audit.','','11.4.11'),
(12715,'Ignore UI modules warnings','','11.4.11'),
(12716,'By default, administration UI modules (views_ui, field_ui, webform_ui, etc.) generate warnings because they are not needed in production. Check this to ignore these warnings if your editors need these modules to manage content.','','11.4.11'),
(12717,'Minimum page cache lifetime (seconds)','','11.4.11'),
(12718,'Minimum recommended value for page cache duration. Pages cached for less time will trigger warnings. Guidelines: High-traffic/static sites: 24 hours (86400) | Medium sites: 6 hours (21600) | Dynamic sites: 1 hour (3600) | Real-time content: 15 min (900)','','11.4.11'),
(12719,'Ignore BigPipe Sessionless warnings','','11.4.11'),
(12720,'When enabled, the audit will not penalize the score for missing the BigPipe Sessionless module (big_pipe_sessionless). Use this for sites where BigPipe Sessionless is intentionally not installed.','','11.4.11'),
(12721,'File extensions to analyze','','11.4.11'),
(12722,'Comma-separated list of file extensions.','','11.4.11'),
(12723,'Recommended:','','11.4.11'),
(12724,'Includes all Drupal-specific extensions: PHP files, module files, install files, theme files, and info.yml. Markdown (.md) files are excluded to avoid false positives from code snippets in fenced blocks.','','11.4.11'),
(12725,'1 - All issues (strictest)','','11.4.11'),
(12726,'2 - Almost all','','11.4.11'),
(12727,'3 - Minor issues and above','','11.4.11'),
(12728,'4 - Moderate issues and above','','11.4.11'),
(12729,'5 - Balanced (recommended)','','11.4.11'),
(12730,'6 - Notable issues and above','','11.4.11'),
(12731,'7 - Important issues only','','11.4.11'),
(12732,'8 - Serious issues only','','11.4.11'),
(12733,'9 - Critical issues only','','11.4.11'),
(12734,'10 - Most critical only','','11.4.11'),
(12735,'Minimum severity level','','11.4.11'),
(12736,'Only report issues with this severity or higher. Lower values show more issues.','','11.4.11'),
(12737,'5 for balanced analysis. Use 1 for strict (all issues), 8+ for critical only.','','11.4.11'),
(12738,'Ignore warnings (only show errors)','','11.4.11'),
(12739,'When enabled, only coding standards errors will be reported. Warnings will be ignored.','','11.4.11'),
(12740,'Keep unchecked to see all issues. Enable only to focus on critical errors first in legacy codebases.','','11.4.11'),
(12741,'Exclude specific rules','','11.4.11'),
(12742,'Select rules to exclude from analysis. Useful for legacy code or specific project requirements.','','11.4.11'),
(12743,'Keep all enabled for new projects. For legacy migrations, temporarily exclude commenting rules.','','11.4.11'),
(12744,'Parallel processes','','11.4.11'),
(12745,'Number of parallel processes for analysis.','','11.4.11'),
(12746,'4-10 depending on server CPU cores. Higher values speed up analysis on large codebases.','','11.4.11'),
(12747,'Enable caching','','11.4.11'),
(12748,'Cache analysis results between runs. Significantly speeds up repeated analysis when only few files change.','','11.4.11'),
(12749,'Maximum violations to display','','11.4.11'),
(12750,'Limits violations shown in results.','','11.4.11'),
(12751,'2000. Set to 0 for unlimited (may slow down the interface with many violations).','','11.4.11'),
(12752,'Report width (characters)','','11.4.11'),
(12753,'Maximum width for code snippets and messages.','','11.4.11'),
(12754,'120 characters.','','11.4.11'),
(12755,'Show sniff codes in results','','11.4.11'),
(12756,'Display the sniff identifier (e.g., Drupal.Commenting.DocComment) with each violation. Useful for understanding which rule was violated and for exclusion configuration.','','11.4.11'),
(12757,'The analyzer auto-detects <code>phpcs</code> and <code>phpcbf</code> from <code>composer.json</code> (<code>config.bin-dir</code>) and the usual <code>vendor/bin/</code> and <code>bin/</code> locations. To use other executables, such as wrapper scripts, set their absolute paths in <code>settings.php</code> with <code>$settings[\'audit_phpcs_binary_path\']</code> and <code>$settings[\'audit_phpcbf_binary_path\']</code>. They cannot be set from this form, so that a configuration change cannot make the server run another program.','','11.4.11'),
(12758,'Paths set in settings.php','','11.4.11'),
(12759,'Binary location','','11.4.11'),
(12760,'Analysis level','','11.4.11'),
(12761,'PHPStan strictness level (0-10). <strong>Recommended: Level 5</strong> for most Drupal projects. Higher levels detect more issues but may report false positives. Start with level 5 and increase gradually as you fix errors.','','11.4.11'),
(12762,'256 MB','','11.4.11'),
(12763,'512 MB (@recommended)','','11.4.11'),
(12764,'1 GB','','11.4.11'),
(12765,'2 GB','','11.4.11'),
(12766,'Maximum memory PHPStan can use during analysis. Increase this if you get \"out of memory\" errors. <strong>Recommended: 512M</strong> for most projects, 1G for large codebases.','','11.4.11'),
(12767,'Maximum errors to display','','11.4.11'),
(12768,'Limit the number of errors shown in the detailed results. Set a lower value for faster page loading if you have many errors.','','11.4.11'),
(12769,'Skip deprecation checks','','11.4.11'),
(12770,'Check this to <strong>ignore</strong> deprecated code detection. <em>Not recommended</em> - deprecation checks help prepare your code for Drupal 11.','','11.4.11'),
(12771,'Skip PHPDoc type inference','','11.4.11'),
(12772,'Check this to <strong>ignore</strong> @var, @param, and @return annotations. <em>Not recommended</em> - Drupal APIs rely heavily on PHPDoc for type information.','','11.4.11'),
(12773,'Skip entity type mapping','','11.4.11'),
(12774,'Check this to <strong>disable</strong> Drupal entity type mapping. <em>Not recommended</em> - entity mapping reduces false positives when working with entities.','','11.4.11'),
(12775,'Ignore Options','','11.4.11'),
(12776,'By default, all recommended analysis features are enabled. Check the options below to <strong>disable</strong> specific features.','','11.4.11'),
(12777,'Active Entity Type Mappings','','11.4.11'),
(12778,'Custom entity mappings','','11.4.11'),
(12779,'Add mappings for custom entity types not listed above. Format: one mapping per line as <code>entity_type_id: Full\\Class\\Name</code>.','','11.4.11'),
(12780,'Entity Type Mapping (Auto-detected)','','11.4.11'),
(12781,'Entity type mappings are automatically detected based on installed modules. PHPStan will use these mappings to better understand your Drupal code.','','11.4.11'),
(12782,'Use the PHPStan configuration of each module and theme','','11.4.11'),
(12783,'Modules and themes that ship a phpstan.neon or phpstan.neon.dist (as drupal.org GitLab CI uses) are analyzed with it: its level, excludes, ignored errors and baseline. The rest of the code uses the settings of this form.','','11.4.11'),
(12784,'Report unmatched ignored errors','','11.4.11'),
(12785,'When enabled, PHPStan will report if any ignored error patterns no longer match any errors. Useful to keep your ignored errors list clean.','','11.4.11'),
(12786,'Error patterns to ignore','','11.4.11'),
(12787,'Patterns of errors to ignore (one per line). Use regular expressions.','','11.4.11'),
(12788,'This is useful for known false positives or errors you plan to fix later.','','11.4.11'),
(12789,'Paths to exclude are configured globally in the <a href=\":url\">main audit settings</a> (exclude patterns). PHPStan uses the same exclude patterns as all other analyzers.','','11.4.11'),
(12790,'Modules to exclude','','11.4.11'),
(12791,'One module name per line. Excluded modules will not be scanned for tests and will not affect the score. Useful for simple helper modules, themes, or generated code that does not require unit testing.','','11.4.11'),
(12792,'Trusted roles','','11.4.11'),
(12793,'Select roles that should be considered trusted (administrators). These roles will not be checked for dangerous permissions. Roles marked as \"Administrator role\" in Drupal are pre-selected by default.','','11.4.11'),
(12794,'Ignore Simple XML Sitemap module check','','11.4.11'),
(12795,'When enabled, the missing Simple XML Sitemap module will not generate errors or affect the score. Use this for sites that use an alternative sitemap solution or do not need XML sitemaps.','','11.4.11'),
(12796,'Ignore sitemap reference in robots.txt','','11.4.11'),
(12797,'When enabled, a missing Sitemap directive in robots.txt will not generate warnings or affect the score.','','11.4.11'),
(12798,'Ignore Metatag module check','','11.4.11'),
(12799,'When enabled, the missing Metatag module will not generate errors or affect the score. Use this for sites where Metatag is intentionally not installed.','','11.4.11'),
(12800,'Ignore Redirect module check','','11.4.11'),
(12801,'When enabled, the missing Redirect module will not generate errors or affect the score. Use this for sites that do not need to manage URL redirects.','','11.4.11'),
(12802,'Ignore Pathauto (module and pattern checks)','','11.4.11'),
(12803,'When enabled, a missing Pathauto module and missing Pathauto patterns will not generate errors or warnings or affect the score for any entity type.','','11.4.11'),
(12804,'Ignore Pathauto checks for Content (nodes)','','11.4.11'),
(12805,'When enabled, missing Pathauto patterns for content types will not affect the score.','','11.4.11'),
(12806,'Ignore Pathauto checks for Taxonomy terms','','11.4.11'),
(12807,'When enabled, missing Pathauto patterns for taxonomy vocabularies will not affect the score.','','11.4.11'),
(12808,'Ignore Pathauto checks for Users','','11.4.11'),
(12809,'When enabled, missing Pathauto patterns for user entities will not affect the score.','','11.4.11'),
(12810,'Ignore Pathauto checks for Media','','11.4.11'),
(12811,'When enabled, missing Pathauto patterns for media entities will not affect the score.','','11.4.11'),
(12812,'Ignore Pathauto by entity type','','11.4.11'),
(12813,'Select specific entity types to exclude from Pathauto pattern checks. Only applies when the global ignore above is disabled.','','11.4.11'),
(12814,'Ignore cache bubbling analysis','','11.4.11'),
(12815,'Skip detection of {{ content }} usage and cache metadata bubbling issues.','','11.4.11'),
(12816,'Ignore anti-patterns analysis','','11.4.11'),
(12817,'Skip detection of performance anti-patterns like drupal_entity(), database queries, etc.','','11.4.11'),
(12818,'Ignore field synchronization analysis','','11.4.11'),
(12819,'Skip detection of fields configured in view modes but not used in templates, and vice versa.','','11.4.11'),
(12820,'Ignore theme suggestions analysis','','11.4.11'),
(12821,'Skip listing of theme hook suggestions registered from custom modules and themes.','','11.4.11'),
(12822,'Ignore preprocess anti-patterns analysis','','11.4.11'),
(12823,'Skip detection of drupal_render() and other anti-patterns in preprocess hooks.','','11.4.11'),
(12824,'Ignore external libraries analysis','','11.4.11'),
(12825,'Skip detection of external CSS/JS libraries in *.libraries.yml files (CDN, unpkg, etc.).','','11.4.11'),
(12826,'Ignore regular updates in scoring','','11.4.11'),
(12827,'Only penalize the score for security updates. Regular (non-security) updates will still be reported but won\'t affect the audit score. Useful for stable projects focused on security maintenance only.','','11.4.11'),
(12828,'Relationships warning threshold','','11.4.11'),
(12829,'Number of relationships in a view display above which a performance warning is shown. Views with many relationships can be slow.','','11.4.11'),
(12830,'Exclude disabled views','','11.4.11'),
(12831,'When checked, disabled (archived) views are ignored entirely: they do not affect the score and are not listed. Uncheck to audit them as well; disabled views are then flagged as such in the listings.','','11.4.11'),
(12832,'Views excluded from cache audit','','11.4.11'),
(12833,'View machine names to exclude from cache-related warnings and scoring (one per line). These views intentionally have no cache configured by design and should not penalize the audit score. Examples: <code>watchdog</code> (real-time logs), <code>redirect_404</code> (404 tracking).','','11.4.11'),
(12834,'Views excluded from anonymous access audit','','11.4.11'),
(12835,'View machine names to exclude from the anonymous access warnings and scoring (one per line), for views whose access is intended or enforced by other means than the view access settings. Example: <code>media_library</code> (its widget routes have their own access check).','','11.4.11'),
(12836,'Ignored log entries','','11.4.11'),
(12837,'Text fragments, one per line. Log entries whose message or message variables contain one of them are left out of the counts, the score and the listings. Use it for known entries that are not defects of the site, such as <code>Attempting to re-run cron while it is already running</code> (Automated Cron overlapping a running cron) or <code>eval()\'d code</code> (errors typed in drush php:eval). The SQL wildcards % and _ are allowed.','','11.4.11'),
(12838,'Audit Submodules Settings','','11.4.11'),
(12839,'Settings for each audit submodule. Adjust parameters and enable or disable specific checks.','','11.4.11'),
(12840,'For uptime monitors and load balancers: the endpoint answers <code>200 OK</code> while every enabled check passes and <code>503 FAIL</code> otherwise. It is never cached and only runs checks that cost next to nothing, so it can be polled often.','','11.4.11'),
(12841,'Endpoint URL','','11.4.11'),
(12842,'Reflects the saved settings. Without the right secret the endpoint answers 404.','','11.4.11'),
(12843,'Secret','','11.4.11'),
(12844,'Requests must pass it as <code>?secret=</code>: the endpoint is never public, because its answer tells which checks fail. At least 16 letters, digits, hyphens or underscores.','','11.4.11'),
(12845,'Minimum score of the Config Checks Audit','','11.4.11'),
(12846,'The check fails when the score of the config checks is lower. 100 fails on any failing or unverifiable check. Leave it empty to leave the audit out.','','11.4.11'),
(12847,'Check that the database answers','','11.4.11'),
(12848,'A page can be served from a cache backend such as Redis without the database, so a successful request alone does not prove it works.','','11.4.11'),
(12849,'Maximum hours since the last cron run','','11.4.11'),
(12850,'Leave it empty to leave cron out.','','11.4.11'),
(12851,'Check that the files directories are writable','','11.4.11'),
(12852,'The public files directory, and the private one when it is configured.','','11.4.11'),
(12853,'Check that the default cache backend works','','11.4.11'),
(12854,'Writes a small entry to the default cache bin and reads it back, which detects an unreachable Redis or Memcache server.','','11.4.11'),
(12855,'Show the time the answer was generated','','11.4.11'),
(12856,'Adds the generation time on a second line. If it does not change between requests, a CDN or proxy in front of the site is caching the answer.','','11.4.11'),
(12857,'Show the result of every check','','11.4.11'),
(12858,'Adds one line per check with OK or FAIL and a short detail, such as the score of an audit against its minimum, to find out what fails. It never says which setting or module is wrong.','','11.4.11'),
(12859,'Health check endpoint','','11.4.11'),
(12860,'Connection successful! DruScan API accepted the test data and it is now today\'s canonical snapshot.','','11.4.11'),
(12861,'The secret must be at least 16 letters, digits, hyphens or underscores.','','11.4.11'),
(12862,'A key is saved. Leave empty to keep it.','','11.4.11'),
