(12868,'1. Install All Recommended Packages','','11.4.11'),
(12869,'Install PHPStan with all recommended Drupal extensions in one command:','','11.4.11'),
(12870,'Package Details','','11.4.11'),
(12871,'2. Reload This Page','','11.4.11'),
(12872,'After installation, reload this page to run the analysis. All configuration options (analysis level, entity mappings, ignored errors, etc.) can be configured from the <a href=\":settings_url\">Audit settings page</a>.','','11.4.11'),
(12873,'Shadowed route','','11.4.11'),
(12874,'Pointing to','','11.4.11'),
(12875,'Findings','','11.4.11'),
(12876,'Alias route shadowing','','11.4.11'),
(12877,'@desc Weighted at @w% in the analyzer total.','','11.4.11'),
(12878,'Alias paths that collide with a static Drupal route (e.g. an alias on /admin or /user/login). The router resolves the route first, so the alias becomes unreachable and the configured target is effectively orphaned.','','11.4.11'),
(12879,'Cycles in the redirect graph of up to @n nodes: direct self-redirects (A → A), 2-node loops (A → B → A) and longer cycles. Any cycle traps the browser in an infinite redirect and breaks the affected URL.','','11.4.11'),
(12880,'Redirect broken destinations','','11.4.11'),
(12881,'Enabled redirects whose destination cannot be resolved: empty URI, malformed entity reference, target entity that has been deleted, route name that no longer exists, or internal path that matches no Drupal route or alias. Visiting these URLs returns a 404.','','11.4.11'),
(12882,'Redirect duplicate sources','','11.4.11'),
(12883,'A single source path mapped by more than one enabled redirect row. Drupal will use whichever row wins the lookup, leaving the others as silent dead config that is hard to audit and easy to break inadvertently when editing one of them.','','11.4.11'),
(12884,'Two situations are reported here: the same alias mapped to several system paths (navigation roulette — the same URL serves different content depending on which row wins) and the same system path with several alternative aliases (content reachable from multiple URLs, which dilutes SEO and confuses link sharing).','','11.4.11'),
(12885,'Alias broken targets','','11.4.11'),
(12886,'Aliases whose system path points to an entity that no longer exists (stale aliases left behind after the original node, term or user was deleted). Unpublished entities are intentionally NOT flagged: an alias may legitimately stay attached to an unpublished entity.','','11.4.11'),
(12887,'Alias formatting issues','','11.4.11'),
(12888,'Aliases with structural problems: empty, missing the leading slash, containing consecutive slashes (//) or exceeding a reasonable length. These typically indicate Pathauto patterns with empty tokens or malformed aliases entered manually.','','11.4.11'),
(12889,'Alias / redirect conflicts','','11.4.11'),
(12890,'Paths that exist both as a redirect source and as a path alias in overlapping languages (the same language, or either one language-neutral). The alias wins and the redirect never fires; this hides bugs because deleting the wrong one looks harmless until the surviving rule is changed. A redirect to the same target as the alias is only reported as a notice and does not lower the score.','','11.4.11'),
