(15920,'No anti-patterns detected in preprocess hooks.','','11.4.11'),
(15921,'All CSS and JS assets are hosted locally. No external CDN dependencies detected.','','11.4.11'),
(15922,'Twig Anti-Patterns','','11.4.11'),
(15923,'Detects problematic patterns in Twig templates: debug functions (kint, dump), drupal_render(), database queries, render array drilling, unsafe |raw filter usage, |t filter on variables, and deprecated entity load functions.','','11.4.11'),
(15924,'Detects entity templates that access fields individually without rendering {{ content }}, which causes cache metadata to not bubble correctly and can lead to stale content.','','11.4.11'),
(15925,'Compares fields used in Twig templates against fields configured in entity view modes. Detects fields configured but not rendered, and fields rendered but not configured.','','11.4.11'),
(15926,'Detects CSS and JS files loaded from external CDNs or URLs in *.libraries.yml files. External resources can cause privacy, performance, reliability, and security concerns.','','11.4.11'),
(15927,'Theme Suggestions','','11.4.11'),
(15928,'Lists custom theme suggestion hooks registered in modules and themes. Informational only, does not affect the audit score.','','11.4.11'),
(15929,'Preprocess Anti-Patterns','','11.4.11'),
(15930,'Detects anti-patterns in preprocess hooks: drupal_render(), renderer service render(), and debug functions (kint, dump) that should not be in production code.','','11.4.11'),
(15931,'Security Issue:','','11.4.11'),
(15932,'Building attributes as strings like <code>&lt;div class=\"base {{ class }}\"&gt;</code> is a <strong>security vulnerability</strong>. If the variable contains user input, it can lead to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attacks because Twig\'s auto-escaping does not protect against attribute injection.','','11.4.11'),
(15933,'Example of attack:','','11.4.11'),
(15934,'If <code>class</code> contains <code>foo\" onclick=\"alert(1)</code>, the resulting HTML would be:','','11.4.11'),
(15935,'Correct approach:','','11.4.11'),
(15936,'Always use Drupal\'s Attributes object which properly escapes all values:','','11.4.11'),
(15937,'The <code>|clean_class</code> filter sanitizes the value, and the Attributes object ensures proper HTML escaping. This also allows contributed modules to add their own attributes safely.','','11.4.11'),
(15938,'Problem:','','11.4.11'),
(15939,'Inline <code>style=\"...\"</code> attributes bypass Drupal\'s CSS aggregation, make theming harder to maintain, and cannot be cached separately.','','11.4.11'),
(15940,'Solution:','','11.4.11'),
(15941,'Move the styles to a CSS file and attach it via a <code>*.libraries.yml</code> library, applying classes to the markup instead of inline styles.','','11.4.11'),
(15942,'The <code>|render</code> filter forces immediate rendering, which can hurt performance on high traffic sites by preventing render caching optimizations.','','11.4.11'),
(15943,'If you need just the value, access it directly via the entity: <code>{{ node.field_name.value }}</code>. If you need to render for cache metadata but access values, use: <code>{% set _cache = content.field_name %}{{ node.field_name.value }}</code>. Alternatively, use Twig Tweak\'s <code>|field_raw</code> filter.','','11.4.11'),
(15944,'Embedding JavaScript directly in Twig templates using <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> tags is a bad practice that harms maintainability:','','11.4.11'),
(15945,'Scripts cannot be aggregated or minified by Drupal\'s asset system','','11.4.11'),
(15946,'JavaScript becomes scattered across multiple template files','','11.4.11'),
(15947,'Cannot leverage browser caching for JS','','11.4.11'),
(15948,'Harder to debug and maintain','','11.4.11'),
(15949,'May cause issues with Content Security Policy (CSP)','','11.4.11'),
(15950,'Move JavaScript to a dedicated file and attach it via a library:','','11.4.11'),
(15951,'Create a JS file in your theme: <code>js/components/my-component.js</code>','','11.4.11'),
(15952,'Define a library in <code>THEME.libraries.yml</code>','','11.4.11'),
(15953,'Attach the library in the template: <code>{{ attach_library(\'THEME/my-component\') }}</code>','','11.4.11'),
(15954,'Use <code>drupalSettings</code> to pass dynamic data from PHP to JavaScript','','11.4.11'),
(15955,'Recommendation:','','11.4.11'),
(15956,'Every Twig template should start with a documentation comment that describes the template\'s purpose and available variables. This improves maintainability and helps other developers understand the template.','','11.4.11'),
(15957,'Add a documentation block like this:','','11.4.11'),
